  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ande Ko&apos; Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to strengthen Paraguays capacity to prevent and process cases of trafficking in persons and to provide protection for victims. The project will target departments and stakeholders in the capital city. The implementer will train network stakeholders on the identification of trafficking victims and victim service provision. The project anticipates holding trainings for participants from the public and private sector and conducting awareness raising events. The implementer will develop comprehensive training manuals for victim care providers and, with the participation of representatives from state institutions and civil society organizations, develop a referral mechanism among victim service providers and government stakeholders. The project will also create a directory of victim care institutions for local networks and stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
